content.text:
Fixed `src/text.js`:

```js
export function truncate(text, max) {
  if (text.length <= max) return text;
  if (max <= 3) return '.'.repeat(Math.max(max, 0));
  return text.slice(0, max - 3) + '...';
}
```

The bug was slicing to `max` then appending `'...'`, giving `max + 3` characters. It now reserves 3 characters for the ellipsis. For `max <= 3` the ellipsis cannot fit alongside any text, so it degrades to dots within the limit (including `max = 0` → `''`). Short-text early return and `capitalize` are untouched; existing tests pass.
